INSERT INTO `entity_versions` (`entity_key`, `kind`, `toon`, `locale`, `json`, `author`, `created_at`, `status`, `message`)
SELECT 'script:catpope:en', 'script', 'catpope', 'en', '{"text":"    # 0. Chapter\\n\\n    # NIGHTMARE\\n    # (Transformation Exorcism)\\n\\n    Scanning a QR Code opens video in the browser.\\n    Alternatively, video stills are shown in the print \\n    edition.\\n\\n1   INT./EXT. VARIOUS LOCATIONS - DAY & NIGHT\\n    \\n    CAT POPE (middle-aged) has a sphynx cat head and a \\n    pope\'s robe. Appears as PLF (Pope-like Figure), \\n    CAT and CAT POPE.\\n\\n    We see CAT POPE in a dream scene. Wandering as \\n    a CAT, in a monastery, hunted, in the snow, in combat, in a \\n    collapsing library, a graveyard. CAT POPE \\n    tries to exorcise a demon from himself.\\n\\n    After the failed attempt, however, CAT POPE \\n    gives up and surrenders to being a CAT. Licks his \\n    paws and comfortably lies down on the ground.\\n\\n---\\n    # 1. Song\\n\\n    # ROAR LITTLE KITTY      \\n\\n    1st Verse   You feel like you \\n                can do anything\\n                and you want to roar.\\n                How did you get lost,\\n                Yet, I am glad that you came,\\n                I give shelter and love here.\\n                            \\n    Chorus      So roar little kitty,\\n                Roar little kitty,\\n                Roar little kitty, roar.\\n\\n    2nd Verse   They tell you, you are losing \\n                your mind.\\n                They are just mocking your pride.\\n                Take all of your anger and fears \\n                and decide!\\n                There are millions of eyes,\\n                but they are blind to my light.\\n                My light, my light.\\n                            \\n    Bridge      Can you feel it?\\n                Now you feel strong.\\n                Like really really really strong.\\n                Close your eyes,\\n                Take a deep breath,\\n                Electricity is running through \\n                your body.\\n---\\n    # 1. Chapter\\n\\n    # DENIAL\\n\\n2   INT. BEDROOM - NIGHT\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.)\\n                A NEW DAY, AN OLD GAME!\\n\\n    The music from [[Roar Little Kitty]] ended abruptly.\\n    PLF woke from a cruel nightmare.\\n    Sweating, PLF sat in bed, we saw the\\n    fear-filled eyes.\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                        (shouted)\\n                MOM! WTF?!\\n\\n    PLF pinched himself.\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                Phew! It was just a dream.\\n\\n    PLF fell asleep again.\\n\\n3   EXT. BRUTALIST APARTMENT BLOCK - SUNRISE\\n    \\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.)\\n                Every morning the sun rose, it was written so. \\n                It shifted, we knew it, depending on the \\n                position of the Earth to  the star, and if it\\n                rained or there was too much fog, \\n                then we could still be sure that behind it, \\n                since the beginning of time, the same cosmic \\n                ritual was taking place. Light followed \\n                shadow, and the light was life, and with life \\n                my day began.\\n\\n                                            ZOOM ON APARTMENT\\n\\n    {BELL RINGS}\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.) (cont\'d)\\n                To make sure this day could work, I set \\n                myself  an alarm, a digital one with \\n                atomic clock connection.\\n\\n\\n4   COMMERCIAL - SCHAFFHAUSEN\\n\\n    Natural trust in cosmic precision and \\n    traditional craftsmanship. Naturally from Schaffhausen. \\n    Order your Chronomat at this promo link \\n    with a 20% discount \\n    https://bit.ly/catpope?code=schaffhausen \\n    Because only the earliest bird catches the worm.\\n\\n5   INT. BEDROOM - SUNRISE\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.)\\n                We preaching beings had the duty to \\n                appear first before the congregations and \\n                perform our own rituals before them. That \\n                was just part of it. It didn\'t bother me.\\n\\n    PLF lay in bed. {RINGING}\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.) (cont\'d)\\n                Yet, I was practiced in skillfully ignoring \\n                this struggle. Yes, practiced in the technique \\n                of Lucid Dreaming, a method in which the \\n                slumber state could be used to control one\'s own \\n                dreams. An incredibly exciting method; it was as \\n                if you were experiencing and writing a movie in \\n                all reality. An indescribable feeling of power. \\n\\n                I forced the ringing into a trill. \\n                It multiplied like on a DMT-trip. \\n\\n                I compressed this further until they \\n                became howling sirens. \\n                The sirens I took again as a sample. \\n                Stabilized them. Drew with them \\n                an invisible layer of Engelhorn trumpets \\n                into the space and made the clouds in the \\n                upper hemisphere oscillate.\\n\\n    CAT appeared at the door to the bedroom. Nonchalantly \\n    it jumped onto the nightstand and struck the \\n    ringing device a fierce blow. It crashed to \\n    the ground. PLF startled and was instantly awake.\\n\\n    Silhouette of PLF in front of the window. Stared out the \\n    window.\\n\\n    CLOSE-UP OF THE FACE\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                I hate Mondays... (TM Garfield)\\n\\n    PLF dragged itself out of the bedroom through the \\n    corridor towards the kitchen.\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                First to the kitchen. Protein!\\n\\n6   INT. KITCHEN\\n\\n    PLF skillfully cracked two eggs simultaneously into a pan.\\n    \\n    {SIZZLE SIZZLE SIZZLE CRACK FIZZ SIZZLE SIZZLE}\\n\\n    Sudden turn. There were skid marks in the air. With \\n    half-closed eyes, PLF went to the toilet. Took a book. \\n    Sat down.\\n\\n7   INT. TOILET\\n\\n    The book was titled: \\"The Decameron\\"\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                        (thought)\\n                Well, a bit trivial, but good for \\n                storytelling.\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                        (continued reading)\\n                He made three rings and gave one to each \\n                son?\\n\\n                A great metaphor that there is not just one \\n                true faith! Interesting, but \\n                dangerous words. Luckily, no one reads \\n                my thoughts. \\n                            \\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.) \\n                I thought!\\n                            \\n                            PLF\\n                Who determines the truth? \\n                Who holds the keys to the stories? \\n                Where lies the difference between my \\n                will and what I stage for others? \\n                Whom should I serve, if not three masters, \\n                the perfect Trinity of Chaos?\\n\\n    {SWOOSH SPLASH}\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.)\\n                Naturally, the reading took longer than I \\n                wanted to admit. I tended to lose myself in \\n                the text. Sucked in, as if I \\n                myself were the maid at the stake.\\n\\n    Background noises\\n    \\n    {FRY FRY FRY SIZZLE}\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                        (pondered)\\n                All fetish? All show? Do I just \\n                want to entertain?\\n\\n    \\"Let me entertain you\\" melody by Robbie Williams \\n    played in the background.\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                No, it\'s about more than the \\n                metaphor! Ignite fires. They should \\n                burn with emotions with me.\\n\\n    {FRY FRY FRY SIZZLE}\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                Oh, shit!\\n\\nQuick exit to the kitchen\\n\\n8   INT. KITCHEN\\n\\n    {FIZZ FIZZ FIZZ SIZZLE}\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                Holy Moly, Guacamole! My eggs!\\n                {GRRR}\\n\\n    PLF took the pan and threw the burnt eggs into\\n    the trash can.\\n\\n    {SPLAT PLOP}\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                I\'ll eat some wafers later.\\n                There are more important things.\\n    \\n9   BATHROOM\\n\\n    Arriving at the sink, PLF grabbed the paste –\\n    the blue elixir extruded out.\\n\\n    {SQUEEZE, PLOP}\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                Missed? WTF! It seems nothing\\n                is working anymore.\\n\\n                            NARRATOR\\n                The second attempt was successful …\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                        (angered towards the narrator)\\n                Thanks, but WE got it\\n                understood. Silence, now, I\\n                concentrate.\\n\\n    PLF began to brush. With the back and forth of the brush. \\n    {SCRUB SCRUB SCRUB SCRUB} PLF stared into the deep \\n    eye rings. PLF seemed to see through itself, spat into the basin {SPLAT} and stared again \\n    with a mad look in the mirror.\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                        (startled)\\n                {ARRRRR} What was that?\\n\\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                        (rubbed his eyes and yet…)\\n                It was there \\n                    Who\\n                        What\\n                            whose, \\n                            a being!\\n                A cat creature? In a bathrobe?\\n\\n                            NARRATOR\\n                Nothing more! As it appeared, it was also \\n                gone.\\n\\n                            PLF\\n                Well, good, she\'s gone, was probably just \\n                imagination.\\n\\n                            CHOIR (O.S.)\\n                Once it means nothing.\\n\\n10   INT. WARDROBE\\n\\n                            NARRATOR (V.O.)\\n                Carefully and with practiced hand I slipped into \\n                the fine gabardine, whose simple white radiated \\n                its pious elegance. Gabardine, with \\n                its diagonally ribbed structure, lay tightly \\n                on the body. Often wrongly dismissed as common, \\n                it differed significantly from \\n                poplin, which was lighter and cross-ribbed. \\n                However, I could not further be distracted by it. \\n                I loved this \\n                ritual. The tying of the laces, the folding \\n                of the sleeves – everything was in place. I felt as \\n               \\n                            PLF\\n                No, it was no longer a role. The \\n                philosophers argued about \\n                identity. \\n\\n                            NARRATOR\\n                Yes, spirituality/theology \\n                was superior. Finally, the confidence that had been \\n                so long awaited flowed through me today. I was ready.\\n\\n    PLF walked out into the hallway.\\n\\n    {PING}\\n\\n    The elevator door opened.\\n    PLF descended from the penthouse in the lift. \\n    {RATTLE RATTLE}\\n\\n                                                ANIMATION AND \\n                                                FADE OUT\\n\\n    PLF stepped out of the house. Low angle shot in face, \\n    the building in the background.\\n\\n    From the black of the sky, the figure faded in.\\n\\n                        PLF\\n                    (thought)\\n            How splendidly the light of dawn shines through \\n            the corridors of the old ship!\\n            Exactly 54 years ago, 5 hours, 15 minutes \\n            we arrived on this planet together! \\n            In the year when Mao Zedong and Ulrike Meinhof \\n            ascended to the Lord, we came down together. \\n            To be honest, they were \\n            actually at pure luck to get to heaven at all. \\n            They were difficult to \\n            to interpret. You have to look twice \\n            you have to look at such people twice. A \\n            youth without God. They themselves probably \\n            wanted to become gods. They were consistent.\\n\\n                        NARRATOR:IN (V.O.)\\n            That would be a great story, wouldn\'t it? \\n            wouldn\'t it? Science fiction just fitted \\n            really well with my self-image.\\n\\n                        CAT\\n            {FAUCH}\\n\\n                        PLF\\n            There you are again?\\n\\n    On the threshold of the stairs, KATZE reappeared in the \\n    corridor. She looked at PLF defiantly.\\n    PLF flung his long limbs awkwardly.\\n\\n    {WHIP WHIP} \\n                            PLF (cont\'d)\\n                Get out of here! Pull the leash! Go you \\n                beast! And  you\'re ugly too. OMG!\\n\\n    {SWOSH} \\n    \\n    KATZE retreated as if it had unlawfully crossed the \\n    shadows of reality unlawfully, kicking \\n    a cloud of dust. In that moment of defence \\n    a feeling came over PLF. She was reminded of the \\n    dystopian heroines from all the narratives, from \\n    sci-fi to the depths of sacred texts - heroes \\n    Heroes who first had to fight their inner demons \\n    demons to find their true identity in a rigid world. \\n    identity in a rigid world. Little did PLF know how much \\n    how much this struggle would become part of her own journey \\n    would become.\\n\\n    PLF walked on, stepping through the meandering paths of the settlement \\n    PLF \\n    There you are again?\\n","meta":{"title":"Cat Pope - Awakening","author":"Tilman Porschütz","status":"DRAFT",